-- title:
--   Rational powers of a pseudo-uniformiser in a valuation ring
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field and $A \subseteq L$ a valuation subring. Suppose given a commutative Noetherian ring $A_0$ (in the same universe as $L$) together with an injective ring homomorphism $\iota : A_0 \to A$, and a subfield $K_0 \subseteq L$, such that the image of $A_0$ in $L$ under $\iota$ followed by the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow L$ is exactly the subset $A \cap K_0$ of $L$; thus $A_0$ presents the ring $A \cap K_0$ and the latter is Noetherian. Suppose moreover that $L$ is algebraic over $K_0$. Finally let $\pi \in A$ be a non-zero element of the maximal ideal of the local ring $A$. The conclusion is that every non-zero $x \in L$ admits a positive integer $N$, an integer $a$ and a unit $u \in A^{\times}$ with
--   $$x^{N} = u \cdot \pi^{a}$$
--   as an identity in $L$, the right-hand side using the integer power $\pi^{a}$ of the non-zero element $\pi$ of $L$. Equivalently, the value group of $A$ lies in the divisible hull of the subgroup generated by the value of $\pi$, i.e. every value is a rational multiple of $v(\pi)$.
--
--   The statement says that under a Noetherian hypothesis on the level $A \cap K_0$ and algebraicity of $L$ over $K_0$, the element $\pi$ is a pseudo-uniformiser whose value generates the value group of $A$ up to rational multiples. It is used in the study of semistable models and coverings of algebraic curves, where depths of points are measured in integer powers of a single chosen element of the maximal ideal; the proof cites [`ValuationSubring.exists_pow_valuation_eq_valuation_algebraMap_of_isAlgebraic`](thm.html#ValuationSubring.exists_pow_valuation_eq_valuation_algebraMap_of_isAlgebraic), which produces, for a non-zero element, a positive power whose value is the value of an element of the base field.
